<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- Tests of the application, mirror of the TVRename project (choix-implementation/organisation-du-code.md). They
       target Windows Forms like it, so that the code under test loads the framework it was built against. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0-windows</TargetFramework>
    <UseWindowsForms>true</UseWindowsForms>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <!-- NU1701 comes from the .NET Framework packages of the application, which reach this project through its
         reference: a debt of the application, left visible, that Phase 2 resolves there
         (suivi-implementation/phase-2-nettoyage-du-code.md). -->
    <WarningsNotAsErrors>NU1701</WarningsNotAsErrors>
    <SonarQubeTestProject>true</SonarQubeTestProject>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="18.11.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="2.9.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="4.0.1">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <!-- VSTest data collector of the "XPlat Code Coverage" collection that the CI runs, whose OpenCover report the
         SonarQube Cloud analysis reads (choix-implementation/outillage.md). -->
    <PackageReference Include="coverlet.collector" Version="10.1.0">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <Using Include="Xunit" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\TVRename\TVRename.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
